# Next.js Code Structure Guidelines

## 1. Project Organization (P0)

1. CRITICAL: Top-level structure:
   ```
   project-root/
   ├── src/             # All source code
   │   ├── app/         # Next.js App Router
   │   ├── components/  # React components
   │   ├── lib/         # Utilities and shared code
   │   └── styles/      # Global styles
   ├── test/            # All test files
   ├── public/          # Static assets
   ├── package.json     # Package definition
   └── tsconfig.json    # TypeScript configuration
   ```

2. REQUIRED: Source directory organization:
   ```
   src/
   ├── app/             # Next.js App Router pages
   │   ├── layout.tsx   # Root layout
   │   ├── page.tsx     # Homepage
   │   └── [feature]/   # Feature routes
   │       ├── page.tsx # Feature page
   │       └── layout.tsx # Feature layout
   ├── components/      # UI components
   │   ├── ui/          # Base components
   │   └── features/    # Feature-specific components
   ├── lib/             # Shared utilities
   │   ├── utils.ts     # General utilities
   │   ├── types.ts     # Shared type definitions
   │   └── constants.ts # Application constants
   └── styles/          # Global styles
       └── globals.css  # Global CSS
   ```

3. ESSENTIAL: Test directory organization:
   ```
   test/
   ├── unit/            # Unit tests
   │   ├── components/  # Component tests
   │   │   └── ui/
   │   │       └── Button.test.tsx  # Component test
   │   └── lib/
   │       └── utils.test.ts        # Utility test
   └── integration/
       └── auth-flow.test.tsx       # Integration test
   ```

## 2. Naming Conventions (P0)

1. CRITICAL: File and directory naming rules:
   - MUST use kebab-case for multi-word directory names: `user-profile/`
   - MUST use kebab-case for utility and configuration files: `form-utils.ts`
   - MUST use PascalCase for component files: `Button.tsx`
   - NEVER use spaces, special characters or brackets in file or directory names
   - REQUIRED to use descriptive, noun-based names for directories
   - File extensions MUST be lowercase

2. REQUIRED: Component naming patterns:
   ```
   components/
   ├── ui/
   │   ├── Button.tsx         # Base component
   │   ├── Card.tsx           # Base component
   │   └── TextField.tsx      # Base component
   └── features/
       ├── auth/
       │   ├── LoginForm.tsx  # Feature component
       │   └── SignupForm.tsx # Feature component
       └── dashboard/
           └── ActivityChart.tsx # Feature component
   ```

3. ESSENTIAL: Test file naming:
   ```
   test/
   ├── unit/
   │   ├── components/
   │   │   └── ui/
   │   │       └── Button.test.tsx  # Component test
   │   └── lib/
   │       └── utils.test.ts        # Utility test
   └── integration/
       └── auth-flow.test.tsx       # Integration test
   ```

## 3. Import Conventions (P0)

1. CRITICAL: Import aliases:
   ```typescript
   // tsconfig.json
   {
     "compilerOptions": {
       "baseUrl": ".",
       "paths": {
         "@/*": ["./src/*"]
       }
     }
   }
   ```

2. REQUIRED: Import organization:
   ```typescript
   // External dependencies first (alphabetical order)
   import { useState } from 'react'
   import { z } from 'zod'
   
   // Internal modules (by path depth, then alphabetical)
   import { Button } from '@/components/ui/Button'
   import { useAuth } from '@/lib/auth'
   
   // Types and styles last
   import type { User } from '@/lib/types'
   import '@/styles/module.css'
   ```

3. ESSENTIAL: Barrel exports:
   ```typescript
   // src/components/ui/index.ts
   export { Button } from './Button'
   export { Card } from './Card'
   export { TextField } from './TextField'
   
   // Usage
   import { Button, Card, TextField } from '@/components/ui'
   ```

## 4. Component Structure (P1)

1. CRITICAL: Component file organization:
   ```typescript
   // src/components/features/auth/LoginForm.tsx
   
   // 1. Imports
   import { useState } from 'react'
   import { Button } from '@/components/ui/Button'
   
   // 2. Types
   interface LoginFormProps {
     onSuccess?: () => void
   }
   
   // 3. Component definition
   export function LoginForm({ onSuccess }: LoginFormProps) {
     // Component logic
     return (
       <form>
         {/* Component JSX */}
       </form>
     )
   }
   ```

2. REQUIRED: Client component annotation:
   ```typescript
   // src/components/features/auth/LoginForm.tsx
   'use client'
   
   import { useState } from 'react'
   // Rest of component
   ```

3. ESSENTIAL: Prop typing:
   ```typescript
   // Direct interface definition
   interface ButtonProps {
     variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'outline'
     size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg'
     isLoading?: boolean
     children: React.ReactNode
   }
   
   // Or using ComponentPropsWithoutRef for HTML element extension
   import { ComponentPropsWithoutRef } from 'react'
   
   interface ButtonProps extends ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'> {
     variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'outline'
     size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg'
     isLoading?: boolean
   }
   ```

## 5. Route Organization (P1)

1. CRITICAL: App Router structure:
   ```
   src/app/
   ├── layout.tsx         # Root layout with shared UI
   ├── page.tsx           # Homepage
   ├── auth/
   │   ├── login/
   │   │   └── page.tsx   # Login page
   │   └── signup/
   │       └── page.tsx   # Signup page
   └── dashboard/
       ├── layout.tsx     # Dashboard layout
       ├── page.tsx       # Dashboard index
       └── settings/
           └── page.tsx   # Settings page
   ```

2. REQUIRED: Route grouping:
   ```
   src/app/
   ├── (marketing)/       # Group for marketing pages
   │   ├── layout.tsx     # Marketing layout
   │   ├── page.tsx       # Homepage
   │   ├── about/
   │   │   └── page.tsx   # About page
   │   └── contact/
   │       └── page.tsx   # Contact page
   └── (app)/             # Group for authenticated app
       ├── layout.tsx     # App layout with auth checks
       ├── dashboard/
       │   └── page.tsx   # Dashboard page
       └── settings/
           └── page.tsx   # Settings page
   ```

3. ESSENTIAL: Route segmentation:
   ```
   src/app/
   ├── [locale]/         # Internationalization segment
   │   ├── layout.tsx    # Layout with language settings
   │   ├── page.tsx      # Home page
   │   └── products/
   │       ├── page.tsx  # Products listing
   │       └── [id]/     # Dynamic product ID segment
   │           └── page.tsx  # Product detail page
   └── api/              # API routes
       └── [...]         # API endpoints
   ```

## 6. State Management (P1)

1. CRITICAL: State organization:
   ```typescript
   // src/lib/store/auth-store.ts
   import { create } from 'zustand'
   
   interface AuthState {
     user: User | null
     isLoading: boolean
     error: string | null
     login: (email: string, password: string) => Promise<void>
     logout: () => Promise<void>
   }
   
   export const useAuthStore = create<AuthState>((set) => ({
     user: null,
     isLoading: false,
     error: null,
     login: async (email, password) => {
       // Implementation
     },
     logout: async () => {
       // Implementation
     },
   }))
   ```

2. REQUIRED: Context providers:
   ```
   src/
   ├── providers/
   │   ├── auth-provider.tsx     # Authentication provider
   │   ├── theme-provider.tsx    # Theme provider
   │   └── providers.tsx         # Combined providers
   ```

3. ESSENTIAL: Server state:
   ```typescript
   // src/lib/queries/products.ts
   import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'
   
   export function useProducts() {
     return useQuery({
       queryKey: ['products'],
       queryFn: async () => {
         const res = await fetch('/api/products')
         return res.json()
       },
     })
   }
   ```

## 7. API Organization (P2)

1. REQUIRED: API route structure:
   ```
   src/app/api/
   ├── auth/
   │   ├── login/
   │   │   └── route.ts  # POST /api/auth/login
   │   └── logout/
   │       └── route.ts  # POST /api/auth/logout
   └── products/
       ├── route.ts      # GET, POST /api/products
       └── [id]/
           └── route.ts  # GET, PUT, DELETE /api/products/[id]
   ```

2. RECOMMENDED: Service layer:
   ```
   src/lib/
   ├── services/
   │   ├── auth-service.ts     # Authentication related functions
   │   └── product-service.ts  # Product management functions
   ```

3. OPTIONAL: API client:
   ```typescript
   // src/lib/api/client.ts
   export async function apiRequest<T>(
     endpoint: string,
     options: RequestInit = {}
   ): Promise<T> {
     const response = await fetch(`/api/${endpoint}`, {
       headers: {
         'Content-Type': 'application/json',
       },
       ...options,
     })
     
     if (!response.ok) {
       throw new Error(`API error: ${response.statusText}`)
     }
     
     return response.json()
   }
   ```

## 8. Configuration Files (P2)

1. REQUIRED: Configuration file organization:
   ```
   project-root/
   ├── .eslintrc.js             # ESLint configuration
   ├── .prettierrc              # Prettier configuration
   ├── next.config.js           # Next.js configuration
   ├── postcss.config.js        # PostCSS configuration
   ├── tailwind.config.js       # Tailwind CSS configuration
   └── tsconfig.json            # TypeScript configuration
   ```

2. RECOMMENDED: Environment variables:
   ```
   project-root/
   ├── .env                     # Default env vars (committed)
   ├── .env.local               # Local overrides (not committed)
   ├── .env.development         # Development env vars (committed)
   └── .env.production          # Production env vars (committed)
   ```

## 9. Migration from Pages to App Router (P2)

1. REQUIRED: Gradual migration approach:
   ```
   src/
   ├── app/                     # New App Router pages
   │   └── new-feature/
   │       └── page.tsx
   └── pages/                   # Legacy Pages Router pages
       ├── index.tsx
       └── old-feature.tsx
   ```

2. RECOMMENDED: Feature flags for router coexistence:
   ```typescript
   // next.config.js
   module.exports = {
     // Both routers enabled during migration
     experimental: {
       appDir: true,
     },
   }
   ``` 